<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-9">9 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Last Allied troops evacuate Gallipoli</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">British troops left Cape Helles, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallipoli-campaign">Gallipoli campaign</a> in an Ottoman victory. The evacuation was the most successful part of an eight-month operation that cost well over 100,000 lives on both sides.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/paris" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/paris.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-29">29 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Zeppelin raid kills civilians in Paris</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/airship">airship</a> bombed eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, killing more than twenty people in the Ménilmontant area. It was the last Zeppelin raid on the city, which strengthened its air defences.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-21">21 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Battle of Verdun begins</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After a massive bombardment, the German army attacked the French fortress city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/verdun">Verdun</a>. The battle lasted ten months and caused some 700,000 casualties, becoming a symbol of French endurance.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-verdun">Battle of Verdun</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-9">9 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Pancho Villa raids Columbus, New Mexico</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Some 500 of Villa's fighters attacked the border town, killing 18 Americans. The US sent General John Pershing on a punitive expedition into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, which failed to catch Villa.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-20">20 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Einstein submits his general theory of relativity</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">'The Foundation of the General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theory-of-relativity">Theory of Relativity</a>' reached the journal Annalen der Physik. It described gravity as the curvature of spacetime and predicted the bending of light, confirmed in 1919.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-24">24 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Irish rebels launch the Easter Rising in Dublin</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Irish Volunteers and the Citizen Army seized the General Post Office and proclaimed an Irish Republic. The Rising was crushed within a week, but the executions that followed turned opinion towards independence.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-29">29 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">British garrison surrenders to the Ottomans at Kut</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After a siege of nearly five months, General Charles Townshend surrendered some 13,000 British and Indian troops at Kut al-Amara in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>. Thousands died in captivity.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-world-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-31">31 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">British and German fleets clash at Jutland</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The largest naval battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> saw the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a> lose more ships and men, but the German High Seas Fleet withdrew to port and rarely ventured out again.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/medina" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/medina.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-5">5 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Arab Revolt against Ottoman rule begins</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussein-bin-ali-king-of-hejaz">Sharif Hussein</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a>, led by his sons, attacked the Ottoman garrison at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a>. Backed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, the revolt helped drive the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-29">29 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Roger Casement is sentenced to death for treason</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Irish nationalist and former British diplomat was condemned for seeking German help for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/easter-rising">Easter Rising</a>. Despite pleas for clemency he was hanged in August.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-1">1 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">British army suffers 57,470 casualties on the first day of the Somme</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After a week-long bombardment, British and French infantry attacked along the Somme. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> lost 57,470 men killed, wounded or missing, the heaviest single-day toll in the British Army's history.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-15">15 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">William Boeing founds his aircraft company in Seattle</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timber">Timber</a> merchant William Boeing incorporated the Pacific Aero Products Company, renamed Boeing Airplane Company the next year. It grew into a leading aerospace maker, builder of the 707 and 747.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/allies" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/allies.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-30">30 July</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">German saboteurs blow up the Black Tom munitions depot</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">German agents set off explosions at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-butler-10th-earl-of-ormond">Black Tom</a> depot in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> Harbor, destroying munitions bound for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a>. The blast shattered windows across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manhattan">Manhattan</a> and damaged the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/statue-of-liberty">Statue of Liberty</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-15">15 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Tanks go into battle for the first time on the Somme</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">British Mark I tanks supported an attack at Flers-Courcelette. Many broke down, but those that advanced showed the potential of armoured warfare.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-16">16 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Margaret Sanger opens the first US birth control clinic</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Margaret Sanger, her sister and a colleague opened a birth control clinic in Brownsville, Brooklyn. Police closed it nine days later, but Sanger's campaign led to the organisation that became Planned Parenthood.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/noemvriana" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/noemvriana.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-1">1 December</a> · Crisis</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/noemvriana">Noemvriana</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Noemvriana were the events of 1 December 1916 (18 November Old Style) in Athens, when Greek royalist troops and militias clashed with British and French forces landed to enforce Allied demands on King Constantine I.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-18">18 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Battle of Verdun ends</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After ten months of fighting, French counter-attacks closed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-verdun">Battle of Verdun</a>. About 700,000 French and German soldiers were killed, wounded or missing, and the front was almost back where it began.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-verdun">Battle of Verdun</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/grigori-rasputin" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/grigori-rasputin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-30">30 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Grigori Rasputin is murdered in Petrograd</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Nobles led by Prince Felix Yusupov killed Rasputin, the mystic whose influence over the imperial family had become a scandal (17 December, Old Style). The murder did not save the monarchy, which fell weeks later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grigori-rasputin">Grigori Rasputin</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrograd">Petrograd</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-delville-wood">Battle of Delville Wood</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Delville Wood was fought from 15 July to 3 September 1916 as part of the Battle of the Somme in northern France.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-jutland">Battle of Jutland</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Jutland, fought on 31 May and 1 June 1916 in the North Sea off Denmark, was the largest naval battle of the First World War, between the British Grand Fleet and the German High Seas Fleet.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/brusilov-offensive" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brusilov-offensive.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Campaign</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/brusilov-offensive">Brusilov Offensive</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Brusilov Offensive was a major Russian attack on the Eastern Front from June to September 1916 during the First World War, led by General Alexei Brusilov along a front of about 480 kilometres.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-birinjiya">Battle of Birinjiya</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Birinjiya was fought in 1916 near El Fasher between a British-led Anglo-Egyptian force and the army of Sultan Ali Dinar of Darfur.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/anglo-qatari-treaty">Anglo-Qatari Treaty</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Anglo-Qatari Treaty of 3 November 1916 was signed by Britain and Abdullah bin Jassim Al Thani after the Ottoman garrison left Qatar during the First World War.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/protocol-of-korce">Protocol of Korçë</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Protocol of Korçë was an agreement signed on 10 December 1916 between the French military commander in the area and Albanian notables during the First World War.</p></div></li></ol></section>
