<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/austro-hungarian-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Austro-Hungarian%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Austro-Hungarian Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Brusilov Offensive breaks the army; Franz Joseph dies in November</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/darfur-sultanate"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Darfur%20Sultanate.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Darfur Sultanate</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Anglo-Egyptian force wins at Birinjiya; Ali Dinar is killed in November</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/german-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/German%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>German Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Verdun and the Somme cost roughly 300,000 German dead without a breakthrough</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/united-kingdom-of-great-britain-and-ireland"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/United%20Kingdom%20of%20Great%20Britain%20and%20Ireland.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Easter Rising in Dublin</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-burundi"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Burundi.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Burundi</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Belgian troops occupy Burundi during the First World War</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/imperialism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Imperialism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Imperialism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Lenin’s Imperialism, the Highest Stage of Capitalism portrays imperialism as monopoly capitalism on a world scale</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/pan-arabism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Pan-Arabism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Pan-Arabism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Sykes–Picot Agreement divides parts of the Mashreq between Britain and France instead of forming an independent Arab state</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/haile-selassie"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Haile%20Selassie.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Haile Selassie</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">After Lij Iyasu is deposed on 27 September, Tafari is proclaimed Crown Prince and Regent Plenipotentiary under Empress Zewditu</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-romania"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Romania.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Romania</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Romania enters the First World War on the Entente side; the Central Powers occupy Wallachia and Bucharest by the end of the year</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/mecca"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mecca.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mecca</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The revolt of Sharif Hussain bin Ali takes Mecca, and he proclaims the Kingdom of Hejaz</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-jutland"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Jutland.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Jutland</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Scheer replaces the ill Admiral von Pohl as commander of the German fleet</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-jutland"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Jutland.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Jutland</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The German Admiralty halts indiscriminate submarine attacks on merchant shipping after neutral protests</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-jutland"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Jutland.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Jutland</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Jellicoe sails from Scapa Flow on 30 May after the Admiralty intercepts Scheer's signal</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-jutland"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Jutland.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Jutland</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Beatty and Hipper meet on 31 May; Indefatigable and Queen Mary are lost in the battlecruiser action</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-jutland"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Jutland.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Jutland</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Jellicoe deploys at 18:15, and the main fleets engage twice before dark</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-jutland"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Jutland.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Jutland</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Scheer breaks through the British rear in the night and the German fleet reaches port</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-jutland"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Jutland.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Jutland</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A German advance into the North Sea is nearly intercepted by the Grand Fleet</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-verdun"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Verdun.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Verdun</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A bombardment by 808 guns opens Operation Judgement on 21 February and German infantry attack in the afternoon</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-verdun"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Verdun.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Verdun</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">German troops enter Fort Douaumont, held by a small maintenance crew</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-verdun"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Verdun.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Verdun</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Germans extend the offensive to the west bank to destroy the French artillery</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-verdun"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Verdun.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Verdun</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Fort Vaux surrenders on 7 June, and the German advance of 23 June reaches Chapelle Sainte-Fine, its furthest point</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-verdun"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Verdun.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Verdun</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Falkenhayn orders the Germans onto the defensive after the failed attack on Fort Souville</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-verdun"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Verdun.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Verdun</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">French marines and colonial infantry recapture Fort Douaumont</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-verdun"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Verdun.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Verdun</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A French offensive under Mangin takes 11,387 prisoners and recovers the ground lost in February</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/dublin"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Dublin.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Dublin</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Easter Rising takes place in the city centre</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/statue-of-liberty"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Statue%20of%20Liberty.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Statue of Liberty</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Black Tom explosion damaged the torch-bearing arm, and the climb to the torch was closed for good</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/jadidism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Jadidism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Jadidism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Jadid-run institutions of learning number over 5,000</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-the-somme"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20the%20Somme.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of the Somme</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The German attack on Verdun begins on 21 February and French divisions meant for the Somme are diverted there</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-the-somme"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20the%20Somme.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of the Somme</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 1 July the British Fourth Army and the French Sixth Army attack the German Second Army after a bombardment that began on 24 June</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-the-somme"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20the%20Somme.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of the Somme</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 14 July the Fourth Army attacks the German second position at Bazentin Ridge after a five-minute hurricane bombardment</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-the-somme"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20the%20Somme.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of the Somme</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 15 September tanks, the Canadian Corps and the New Zealand Division make their debut on the Somme at Flers–Courcelette</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-the-somme"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20the%20Somme.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of the Somme</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The last big British operation of the year, the Battle of the Ancre, is fought from 13 to 18 November</span></li></ul></section>
